 The series itself is easy to calculate  $(f(x)=\sqrt[5]{3}+\frac{2x^3}{5\cdot \sqrt[5]{3^4}}-\frac{8x^6}{75\cdot \sqrt[5]{3^4}}\dots)$ , but I can't find any ways to represent it as a sum. Thanks in advance for any help.  

Answer: Let [] denote areas and [ABCD] =  $1$ . Note that BPX and CDX are similar, which yields  $\frac{PX}{XC}=\frac{BX}{XD}=\frac13$ . Then, the shaded area is 
 \begin{align}
[\text{Shaded}] &= [BPX] + [CXD] \\
& = \frac{PX}{PC} [BPC]+ \frac{XD}{BD} [BDC] \\
& =\frac14\cdot \frac16 + \frac34\cdot \frac12= \frac5{12}\\
\end{align} 
